    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0762",
      "reading_order": 981,
      "severity": "caution",
      "content": "CAUTION: Some parts are sensitive to electrostatic discharge (ESD). Always perform service",
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 135.0,
        "t": 316.53499,
        "r": 172.75,
        "b": 304.94499
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0207",
      "reading_order": 983,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 182.0500714686394,
        "t": 320.5829162597656,
        "r": 201.5466153916895,
        "b": 299.3404846191406
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0207.png",
      "decorative": true,
      "width": 19,
      "height": 21,
      "image_hash": "1220257455e140c822b978ff384a9a72b7962eb60ba22e7947cafcc48c407ada",
      "next_block_id": "txt_0764"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0764",
      "reading_order": 984,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 135.0,
        "t": 297.92,
        "r": 540.7700400000001,
        "b": 262.3299999999999
      },
      "content": "work at an ESD-protected workstation or mat. If an ESD workstation or mat is not available, touch the sheet-metal chassis to provide a static ground before touching an ESD-sensitive assembly. Protect the ESD-sensitive assemblies by placing them in ESD pouches when they are out of the printer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0765",
      "reading_order": 985,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 135.00004,
        "t": 252.92000000000007,
        "r": 539.6300400000002,
        "b": 217.32999999999993
      },
      "content": "If the replacement part is a roller or pad, avoid touching the spongy part of it. Skin oils on the roller or pad can cause paper pickup and/or print-quality problems. HP recommends using disposable gloves when handling rollers or pads or washing your hands before touching rollers or pads."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0766",
      "reading_order": 986,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 135.0,
        "t": 207.91999999999996,
        "r": 532.73,
        "b": 184.32999999999993
      },
      "content": "IMPORTANT: Make sure that all of the shipping materials (for example shipping tape) are removed from the replacement part prior to installation."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0767",
      "reading_order": 987,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 113.0,
        "t": 173.41999999999996,
        "r": 334.02,
        "b": 161.83000000000004
      },
      "content": "To install an assembly, reverse the removal steps."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0768",
      "reading_order": 988,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 135.00002,
        "t": 152.41999999999996,
        "r": 542.6100400000003,
        "b": 116.83000000000004
      },
      "content": "When applicable, special installation instructions are provided for an assembly at the end of the removal procedure. Always completely read the removal instructions and follow all special installation instructions."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0769",
      "reading_order": 989,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 91.00004,
        "t": 107.41999999999996,
        "r": 339.5900400000002,
        "b": 95.83000000000004
      },
      "content": "Install the white backing (M527/E52545/M528/E52645)."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0770",
      "reading_order": 990,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 113.00002,
        "t": 86.41999999999996,
        "r": 461.4500200000001,
        "b": 74.83000000000004
      },
      "content": "Verify that the springs are positioned correctly on the replacement retention clips."
    }
  ],
